Kite Boarding</i></b></font></p>
<p align="center"><font size="7" color="#FFFFFF"><b><i>2013</i></b></font></p>

<div align="center">
  <center>
  <table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="800" id="table610">
    <tr>
      <td width="100%">
      <p align="center"><i><font size="7" color="#FF0000">The Skydog 
		Report</font></i></p>
		<p align="center">
		<font face="Monotype Corsiva" size="5" color="#66CCFF">October 21 </font>
		<font face="Monotype Corsiva" size="5" color="#FFCC66">was our last of a 
		three day run. Wednesday, Friday and Monday were all great sailing days 
		at Rondeau Bay. I sailed a 6.3 Ezzy sail on my Hi-Tec 9 foot board and 
		was overpowered sometimes but it kept me going through the lulls. Les 
		Squires was on his 4.2 most of the time and on a 5.0 sometimes and he 
		was hard to catch. Don Ferguson favoured his 5.5 sail and had a blast. I 
		took a few photos and a video on Monday so take a look.</font></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>
  <p align="center">&nbsp;</p>
  </center>
</div>

