<p align="center" style="margin-top: -12">&nbsp;</p>

<div align="center">
  <center>
  <table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="800" id="table639">
    <tr>
      <td width="100%">
      <p align="center"><i><font size="7" color="#FF0000">The Skydog 
		Report</font></i></p>
		<p align="center">
		<font face="Monotype Corsiva" size="5" color="#FFCC66">September 10, 
		2013 the forecast was calling for 18 to 22 mph SW&nbsp; winds so Maureen 
		and I headed to Rondeau Bay for a day of fun. We arrived at 10:30 AM and 
		the whitecaps were looking good so I set up and Maureen got on the water 
		around eleven. There were five or more kiters already sailing and Don 
		Ferguson was sailing his windsurfer way down the bay towards Lake Erie. 
		Maureen was taking it easy as she had not been sailing for two years so 
		she stayed in the shallow water inside the pier for a couple of hours. I 
		got on the water about 11:30 and found that my 6.3 Ezzy sail was just 
		right and I headed across the bay and back with steady winds of about 18 
		mph. Finally Maureen took a run with me and she did great doing a water 
		start in the deep half way across. Our friend Les Squires opted to sail 
		at Long Beach a hundred miles east near Welland, Ontario, Canada and Les 
		had a great day too. Friend and kiter John Smith arrived shortly after 
		us and John has mastered&nbsp; kite boarding with finesse. Later in the day 
		there were about ten kiters and seven windsurfers and having a great 
		time on the water.</font></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>
  </center>
</div>

